ies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/capo":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/capo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The capo element indicates at which fret a capo should be placed on a fretted instrument. This changes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"open tuning of the strings specified by staff-tuning by the specified number of half-steps."}],"title":"capo","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/capo","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"capo"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol"}}}